-- title:
--   Unique tangent morphism attached to two lifts, flat case
-- statement:
--   Let $T'$ be an Artinian local ring with residue field $k =$ `ResidueField T'`, and let $I \subseteq T'$ be an ideal with $I \le \mathfrak m_{T'}$ and $I\cdot\mathfrak m_{T'} = 0$. Let $V$ be a $k$-vector space (with the two-sided, centrally acting module structure and a compatible $T'$-action through $k$), and let $\iota : V \to T'$ be an injective $T'$-linear map whose image is exactly $I$. Let $C$ be a flat commutative $T'$-algebra, and write $IC = I\cdot C$ for the ideal generated by the image of $I$. Let $Y$ be a scheme with a morphism $q_Y : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} T'$, and let $u, v : \operatorname{Spec} C \to Y$ be two morphisms, each composing with $q_Y$ to the structure morphism $\operatorname{Spec} C \to \operatorname{Spec} T'$, and agreeing after restriction along $\operatorname{Spec}(C/IC) \to \operatorname{Spec} C$. Then there is exactly one morphism $w$ from $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the thickening $(k \otimes_{T'} C)\otimes_k (k \oplus V)$ (the trivial square-zero extension of $k$ by $V$) to $Y$ satisfying `IsTangentOfPair I V ι C u v w`, i.e. such that there exist a ring homomorphism $\vartheta$ from the equaliser subring $\{(a,b) \in C \times C : a \equiv b \bmod IC\}$ to that thickening which is a Schlessinger map — it sends $(a,a)$ to $\bar a \otimes 1$ and $(0, \iota(\nu)c)$ to $\bar c \otimes \mathrm{inr}(\nu)$ for $\nu \in V$, $c \in C$ — together with a morphism $\varphi : \operatorname{Spec}\{(a,b)\} \to Y$ restricting along the two projections to $u$ and to $v$, and with $w = \operatorname{Spec}\vartheta$ followed by $\varphi$.
--
--   This is the scheme-theoretic form, on a flat affine chart, of Schlessinger's comparison of two lifts of a morphism over a small extension: two lifts agreeing modulo $I$ differ by a unique tangent field valued in the $V$-thickening of the special fibre. It is used downstream to produce tangent coordinates for pairs of lifts (`exists_injective_isTangentOfPair_of_flat`, `exists_isTangentCoordsOfPairAt` and its variants).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_SmallExtension_existsUnique_isTangentOfPair_of_flat.lean

